Minimal variant of hyprlock-fprint-reinit.patch — points 4 + 5 only.

Scope (vs. the full patch):
  KEPT:    MATCH_DISCONNECTED -> scheduleReinit() (point 4) and the
           scheduleReinit()/reinitDevice() recovery engine (point 5), plus a
           one-line reset of the reinit counter on a successful VerifyStart so
           the budget renews after each recovery within a long locked session.
  DROPPED: point 1 (3s delay on resume — no resume-time USB reset in the
           current config, so no firmware-boot window to wait out),
           point 2 (no-match budget 3->10 — fixed by re-enrolling),
           point 3 (MATCH_UNKNOWN_ERROR -> reinit — 1x ever, during verify),
           point 6 (reinit on claim/VerifyStart failures).

Behavioural note: because point 6 is dropped, scheduleReinit() is invoked
exactly once per disconnect (from MATCH_DISCONNECTED). That gives a single
reinit attempt at +3s — which matches the confirmed 21:08 (2026-06-12)
recovery for a long-sleep re-enumeration. The multi-attempt 3s/40s backoff
chain in scheduleReinit() is therefore present but only exercised if a future
trigger re-invokes it; it will NOT self-heal a wedged fprintd on its own here.
If that case ever appears in logs, add back the claimDevice/VerifyStart
failure -> scheduleReinit hooks from the full patch.

Enable by uncommenting the overrideAttrs block in packages.nix and pointing
it at this file.

